Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 03:27:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Icons keep their shape

Icons were stretched or blown up in a few places:
- A picture's size was capped one side at a time, so a large or very small non-square drawing
  was squashed. It is now scaled as a whole.
- Icons turned into one-colour lines (a tint, or apps the pack doesn't have shown as lines) squeezed
  a wide logo into a square. They now keep its shape.
- Tinted pack drawings, a pack's frame for apps it doesn't have, and the icons in a folder's
  card were all drawn into squares whatever their shape. They now fit inside, in proportion.
- With Edge to edge on, a drawing on nothing (an icon pack's line art, a logo with no
  background) was trimmed to its lines and blown up to fill the card, cutting it off. It is now
  shown whole, in the middle of the card with a margin; icons with their own background still
  fill the card.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
